\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The same fixed-DoA errors placed on the hemisphere. The bias vectors point inward, toward the subsector centres from which the anchor of \eqref  {eq:anchor} is built: the magnitude-weighted probability of pointing inward is $0.836$ and the magnitude-weighted mean cosine is $+0.536$. Structure along $\theta = 60^\circ $ is partly geometric and partly the codebook band boundary, and the two cannot be separated with a single codebook.}}{13}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spatialmap}{{5}{13}{The same fixed-DoA errors placed on the hemisphere. The bias vectors point inward, toward the subsector centres from which the anchor of \eqref {eq:anchor} is built: the magnitude-weighted probability of pointing inward is $\fdPin $ and the magnitude-weighted mean cosine is $+\fdBiasCos $. Structure along $\theta = \elevSplit \degs $ is partly geometric and partly the codebook band boundary, and the two cannot be separated with a single codebook}{figure.caption.8}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Stage-by-stage recomposition of the estimator over $10{,}000$ single-jammer queries (PH5). Anchor alone, anchor plus learned offset, and the full output are scored against the same truths. The recomposition is exact: summing the stages reproduces the forward pass to machine precision, so the comparison is an attribution and not an ablation retrained per stage.}}{13}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:decomp}{{6}{13}{Stage-by-stage recomposition of the estimator over $\decompN $ single-jammer queries (PH5). Anchor alone, anchor plus learned offset, and the full output are scored against the same truths. The recomposition is exact: summing the stages reproduces the forward pass to machine precision, so the comparison is an attribution and not an ablation retrained per stage}{figure.caption.9}{}}
